physics-open-problems-AI — licensing and attribution
====================================================

The following licenses apply to the original materials in this repository, to
the extent that the contributors hold rights they can license. The same
division applies to files distributed in the downloadable project archives.

1. Papers and documentation — CC BY 4.0

   Manuscript PDFs and their LaTeX sources, research reports, README prose,
   and original figures in these documents are licensed under Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), unless separately credited.
   You may copy, redistribute, translate, and adapt this material, including
   commercially. When sharing it, give appropriate credit, link to the license,
   retain supplied notices, and indicate changes (including a translation).
   If supplied, link to the source where reasonably practicable. An adapted
   work must not imply endorsement by the original authors or publisher.

   Full legal text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt
   Canonical URL: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Suggested credit: give the work's title, the byline as printed, the project
   URL, and the license. For unsigned repository documentation, cite the
   document title and rongyulin/physics-open-problems-AI as its source.
   A translation or adaptation can add “Translated/adapted by [name]; [changes].”
   For manuscripts signed “Chatgpt”, use that spelling in the credit.

2. Proofs and software — MIT

   Original Lean proof modules, example and test code, and Python, shell and
   other build or verification scripts are licensed under the MIT License.
   You may use, modify, merge, distribute, sublicense, and sell copies of
   the software. Include the copyright and permission notices in all copies
   or substantial portions of the software. Include LICENSES/MIT.txt when
   you redistribute a standalone source file. Research citations are welcome.

   Full text and copyright notice: LICENSES/MIT.txt
   https://opensource.org/license/mit

3. Scope

   Third-party quotations, figures, software, and dependencies retain their
   own notices and licenses. Being cited, imported or referenced in a dependency
   manifest does not relicense an external work. These licenses apply to
   protectable expression. Mathematical statements and methods can be used
   independently; scholarly citation is encouraged when building on a result.
   The licenses grant no permissions to push changes to the GitHub repository.

中文说明
========

本仓库及其工程压缩包按材料类型授权，以贡献者有权许可的内容为限。

1. 论文与文档采用 CC BY 4.0。范围包括原创论文 PDF、LaTeX 源稿、研究报告、
   README 正文和文中另无署名说明的原创图表。允许转载、翻译、改编及商用。
   公开分享时请适当署名，附许可链接，保留已提供的声明，在合理可行时
   链接原作，并标明翻译或其他修改。建议注明题名、原稿所列署名、项目链接
   和许可。对未单独署名的说明，可用文档题名和仓库名作为出处。
   许可全文见 LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt。

2. 原创代码采用 MIT，包括 Lean 证明、示例和测试、Python 验证脚本及
   Shell 等构建脚本。可以复用、修改、再发布、再许可及商用。分发代码副本
   或其中实质部分时，请随附原版权和许可声明。单独转发源文件时可附上
   LICENSES/MIT.txt，其中包含完整声明。欢迎在使用研究成果时引用原项目。

3. 第三方引文、图片、代码和依赖保留其原有声明及许可。上述许可适用于
   受保护的具体表达。独立使用数学命题或方法时，欢迎按学术惯例注明来源。
   仓库写入权限由 GitHub 协作设置管理。
